    "question": "John and his two brothers decide to split the cost of an apartment.  It is 40% more expensive than John's old apartment which costs $1200 per month.  How much does John save per year by splitting the apartment compared to living alone?",
    "gold": "7680",
    "answer": "His old apartment cost 1200*12=$<<1200*12=14400>>14,400 per year\nHis new apartment 1200*1.4=$<<1200*1.4=1680>>1680 per month\nThat means it cost 1680/3=$<<1680/3=560>>560 per month\nSo it cost 560*12=$<<560*12=6720>>6720\nSo he saves 14400-6720=$<<14400-6720=7680>>7680\n#### 7680"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how much John saves per year by splitting the apartment with his two brothers, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the cost of the new apartment.\n2. Determine John's monthly cost if he were to live alone.\n3. Determine John's monthly cost if he splits the apartment with his two brothers.\n4. Calculate the monthly savings by splitting the apartment.\n5. Convert the monthly savings to an annual savings.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the cost of the new apartment.**\n\nThe new apartment costs 40% more than John's old apartment, which costs $1200 per month. Therefore, the cost of the new apartment is:\n\\[ 1200 + 0.4 \\times 1200 = 1200 + 480 = 1680 \\text{ dollars per month} \\]\n\n**Step 2: Determine John's monthly cost if he were to live alone.**\n\nIf John were to live alone, his monthly cost would be the cost of the new apartment, which is $1680.\n\n**Step 3: Determine John's monthly cost if he splits the apartment with his two brothers.**\n\nSince John and his two brothers are splitting the cost of the apartment, each person's share of the monthly cost is:\n\\[ \\frac{1680}{3} = 560 \\text{ dollars per month} \\]\n\n**Step 4: Calculate the monthly savings by splitting the apartment.**\n\nThe monthly savings by splitting the apartment is the difference between John's old monthly cost and his new monthly cost:\n\\[ 1200 - 560 = 640 \\text{ dollars per month} \\]\n\n**Step 5: Convert the monthly savings to an annual savings.**\n\nThe annual savings is the monthly savings multiplied by 12:\n\\[ 640 \\times 12 = 7680 \\text{ dollars per year} \\]\n\nTherefore, the amount John saves per year by splitting the apartment compared to living alone is:\n\\[ \\boxed{7680} \\]",
